### Formal Patent Description

An apparatus comprises a mixing chamber (2) having an upper portion and a lower portion. A top inlet hose (4) is in fluid communication with the upper portion of the mixing chamber (2), and a bottom outlet (23) is provided at the lower portion of the mixing chamber (2). A sieve (16) is arranged within, or in fluid communication with, the mixing chamber (2) for separating particulate material from a fluid passing therethrough. A pump system (18) is fluidly coupled to the mixing chamber (2) and is configured to circulate, introduce, and/or discharge fluid relative to the mixing chamber (2).

The apparatus further comprises an air manifold assembly (8). The air manifold assembly (8) includes a manifold (10), at least one nozzle (12) fluidly coupled to the manifold (10), and a cover (14) disposed over at least a portion of the manifold (10) and/or the nozzle (12). The air manifold assembly (8) is configured to introduce air into the mixing chamber (2) through the at least one nozzle (12), thereby promoting agitation, aeration, or mixing of material contained within the mixing chamber (2).

### Exemplary Independent Claim

1. An apparatus comprising:  
   a mixing chamber (2);  
   an inlet hose (4) fluidly communicating with an upper portion of the mixing chamber (2);  
   an outlet (23) disposed at a lower portion of the mixing chamber (2);  
   a sieve (16) arranged to filter material conveyed through the apparatus;  
   a pump system (18) fluidly coupled to the mixing chamber (2); and  
   an air manifold assembly (8) comprising:  
   a manifold (10);  
   at least one nozzle (12) in fluid communication with the manifold (10); and  
   a cover (14) disposed over at least a portion of the air manifold assembly (8),  
   wherein the air manifold assembly (8) is configured to discharge air through the at least one nozzle (12) to agitate material within the mixing chamber (2).
